Script lookup probes the playbook's own `_scripts/` before any discovery root's, so a name carried by
both resolves to the playbook-local copy. This case and
`a-root-script-runs-when-the-playbook-carries-none` differ only in that copy's presence; the marker
each script writes says which one ran.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-hooks
title: Hooks
summary: Hook-bearing fixture for playbook-transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  only: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: noted
            when: the note is written
            hooks: ["script note"]
      noted: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/only/prompt.md --
---
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/_scripts/note --
#!/bin/sh
echo "playbook" >> "$BOOPING_WORKDIR/note.log"
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/_scripts/note --
#!/bin/sh
echo "root" >> "$BOOPING_WORKDIR/note.log"
-- fixtures/cwd/run/.keep --
-- cmd --
chmod +x ../home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/_scripts/note ../home/Claude/_playbooks/_scripts/note
booping playbook-transition fx-hooks intaking --workdir run
booping playbook-transition fx-hooks noted --workdir run
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
created index.md
not-started → intaking
frontmatter: status=intaking
intaking → noted
frontmatter: status=noted
script note: ok
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/run/note.log --
playbook
